WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.857
Welcome to Web Development Fundamentals. First: what happens when you open a website?

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.825
You type an address, called a URL, into your browser.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.157
A computer called a server sends back the files for that page.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:18.731
Your browser reads the files, and draws the page on your screen.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.148
HTML gives the content and structure: headings, text and images.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.396
CSS controls the look: colours, fonts and layout.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.924
And JavaScript adds behaviour, like buttons that respond.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:42.711
Before you move on, check: Explain what a browser and a server do. Name the job of HTML, CSS and JavaScript. Install a code editor.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.680
In the next lesson: HTML structure.
